          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Philip and Amy spent $200 000 on a luxury car 7 years ago. Its current value is $104 350.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Using the declining-balance method, find the annual percentage depreciation rate over this period.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Answer correct to one decimal place.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$8.9\\%$ p.a.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}S&=V_0(1-r)^n\\\\104350&=200000(1-r)^7\\\\(1-r)^7&=\\frac{104350}{200000}\\\\r&=1-\\sqrt[7]{\\frac{104350}{200000}}\\end{align*}$$\nThe annual depreciation rate is $100\\left(1-\\sqrt[7]{\\frac{104350}{200000}}\\right)\\%=8.9\\%$ p.a., correct to one decimal place.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 32
  },
